      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The One Where She Gets a Family</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;"There seems to be some sort of celebration on the beach.â€&lt;br /&gt;Glimmer, Bow, and Adora immediately rush to the window- forgetting their breakfasts in their hands as they place themselves onto the glass and practically leave a mark in the frame, gasping and cooing as they catch a glance at the gatherings happening on the shore.&lt;br /&gt;â€œTheyâ€™re cats!â€ Bow pipes, voice melting into a godawful coo.&lt;br /&gt;â€œLike literal cats?â€ Catra quirks her brow, â€œyeah no- weâ€™re leaving. Iâ€™m not dealing with an island of cats today.â€&lt;br /&gt;She can predict that Bow and Glimmer will practically force her to do the photoshoot with the furry, mangy things, not to say she wasnâ€™t her own furry, mangy thing- she had never particularly resonated with cats. Other cats, per say,  Melog senses the thought and growls in her presence.&lt;br /&gt;â€œNo, Catra,â€ Adora says in awe, â€œtheyâ€™re like you.â€&lt;br /&gt;***&lt;br /&gt;When the Best Friend Squad finally goes on that intergalatic roadtrip, they make a few pitstops around Etheria first. When they stumble upon an island thatâ€™s cut off all connection to the outside world, what happens when Catra finds out they all look just like her?&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
